      "id": "l3i24-q1b",
      "number": "1(b)",
      "text": "Find the shaded area under y = 24x(2x² – 3)³ between x = –1 and x = 0.",
      "marks": 2,
      "gradeLevel": "merit",
      "topics": [
        "integration",
        "area-under-curves",
        "integration-techniques"
      ],
      "answerType": "working",
      "expectedAnswer": "Use substitution u = 2x²–3",
      "markingGuide": "Step 1: ∫ 24x(2x²–3)³ dx.\n\nStep 2: u = 2x²–3, du = 4x dx.\n\nStep 3: ∫ 6u³ du = 6u⁴/4 = 3u⁴/2.\n\nStep 4: [3(2x²–3)⁴/2] from –1 to 0.\n\nStep 5: At 0: 3(–3)⁴/2 = 3(81)/2 = 121.5.\n\nStep 6: At –1: 3(–1)⁴/2 = 1.5.\n\nStep 7: Area = |121.5–1.5| = 120.\n\nFinal answer: Use substitution u = 2x²–3."
    },
    {
      "id": "l3i24-q1c",
      "number": "1(c)",
      "text": "An object has velocity v(t) = 15⁴√t m/s. Initially 400 m from point Q. Find distance from Q when v = 150 m/s.",
      "marks": 2,
      "gradeLevel": "excellence",
      "topics": [
        "integration",
        "definite-integrals"
      ],
      "answerType": "working",
      "expectedAnswer": "1,200,400 m",
      "markingGuide": "Step 1: s = ∫ 15t^(1/4) dt = 15×(4/5)t^(5/4) + c = 12t^(5/4) + c.\n\nStep 2: At t=0: s=400, c=400.\n\nStep 3: When v=150: 15t^(1/4)=150, t^(1/4)=10, t=10000.\n\nStep 4: s = 12(10000)^(5/4)+400 = 12×100000+400 = 1,200,400 m."
    },
    {
      "id": "l3i24-q1d",
      "number": "1(d)",
      "text": "Solve dy/dx = 12cos(3x)sin(x), given y = 2 when x = π/6. Find y when x = π/3.",
      "marks": 2,
      "gradeLevel": "excellence",
      "topics": [
        "differential-equations",
        "trig-integration"
      ],
      "answerType": "working",
      "expectedAnswer": "y = –1 at x = π/3",
      "markingGuide": "Step 1: Use product-to-sum: cos(3x)sin(x) = (1/2)[sin(4x) – sin(2x)], so 12cos(3x)sin(x) = 6sin(4x) – 6sin(2x).\n\nStep 2: Integrate: y = –(6/4)cos(4x) + (6/2)cos(2x) + c = –(3/2)cos(4x) + 3cos(2x) + c.\n\nStep 3: At x = π/6: –(3/2)cos(2π/3) + 3cos(π/3) + c = –(3/2)(–1/2) + 3(1/2) + c = 3/4 + 3/2 + c = 9/4 + c = 2, so c = –1/4.\n\nStep 4: At x = π/3: y = –(3/2)cos(4π/3) + 3cos(2π/3) – 1/4 = –(3/2)(–1/2) + 3(–1/2) – 1/4 = 3/4 – 3/2 – 1/4 = –1.\n\nFinal answer: y = –1 at x = π/3."
    },
