    {
      "id": "l3i24-q2c",
      "number": "2(c)",
      "text": "Solve dy/dx = 6y²e^(3x), given y = 0.5 when x = 0. Find y when x = 1.",
      "marks": 2,
      "gradeLevel": "excellence",
      "topics": [
        "differential-equations",
        "integration-techniques"
      ],
      "answerType": "working",
      "expectedAnswer": "y ≈ –0.028",
      "markingGuide": "Step 1: Separate variables: ∫y^(–2) dy = ∫6e^(3x) dx.\n\nStep 2: So –1/y = 2e^(3x) + c.\n\nStep 3: At x = 0, y = 0.5: –1/0.5 = –2 = 2·1 + c = 2 + c, so c = –4.\n\nStep 4: Thus –1/y = 2e^(3x) – 4.\n\nStep 5: At x = 1: –1/y = 2e³ – 4 ≈ 40.171 – 4 = 36.171.\n\nStep 6: Therefore y ≈ –1/36.171 ≈ –0.0277.\n\nFinal answer: y ≈ –0.028."
    },
